+
+``--video-triple`` (``--vo=gpu-next`` only)
+    Display three horizontal copies of the video (default: no). Reuses the
+    renderer's frame cache instead of creating a triple-width decoded frame.
+    The option can be changed during playback, for example with the input binding
+    ``Ctrl+3 cycle video-triple``. Each copy keeps the video's current aspect
+    ratio, crop and rotation. Window-relative subtitles and OSD are drawn once
+    over the combined output. Video screenshots include all three copies.
 
